11. (MC) **(MCQ)** In **kernel density estimation (KDE)** using a kernel $K$ and bandwidth $h$, the **mean integrated squared error (MISE) optimal bandwidth** $h^*$ depends on the sample size $n$. How does $h^*$ typically scale with $n$ for smooth densities?

    A) n^{-0.2}
    B) n^{-1/2}
    C) \log(n)/n
    D  n^{-1.5}
    E) n^{-1.0}
